course: dictionary
lesson: 14198
title: The word motorcycle
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A motorcycle is a heavy vehicle with two wheels and an engine. You ride it like a bicycle, but it goes much faster and does not need pedals. «The motorcycle roared down the road.» The word roared tells you the engine was loud, so it was a motorcycle, not a bicycle.
explain: As a verb, to motorcycle means to travel on a motorcycle. «Mia wants to motorcycle across the desert when she is older.» This is less common than the noun, so look at the clues: she wants to travel, and the motorcycle is the vehicle she will use.
explain: Maths can use motorcycles too. «Each motorcycle has 2 wheels.» If you have 4 motorcycles, count 2 wheels for each one. That makes 8 wheels altogether, which is 4 groups of 2.
fact: A motorcycle is a heavy two-wheeled vehicle with an engine.
fact: «Motorcycle» is a noun: a motorcycle, two motorcycles.
fact: «Motorbike» and «bike» are short forms. «Motorbike» is used in the UK and Australia.
fact: Riders on the road must wear a helmet and have a licence.
fact: A motorcycle has 2 wheels, so 5 motorcycles have 10 wheels altogether.
exercise: «The motorcycle roared past the school gate.» What is a motorcycle? | A car with four wheels and no engine | A bicycle with a basket | A small boat with a sail | *A heavy two-wheeled vehicle with an engine
exercise: «Each motorcycle has 2 wheels. How many wheels do 4 motorcycles have?» | 6 | 2 | 10 | *8
exercise: Leo says a motorcycle is a bike, so it must have pedals. Is he right? | *No, a motorcycle has an engine, so it does not need pedals to move | Yes, but only when it rains | Yes, every motorcycle has pedals | No, because it has four wheels
test: «Mum will motorcycle to work on Monday.» What does motorcycle mean in this sentence? | To buy a new car | To fix a bicycle | *To travel on a motorcycle | To ride a horse
test: «Ben put on his ___ before he rode the motorcycle.» Which word fits the gap? | *A helmet | A kite | An umbrella | A sandwich
exam: Which two things must a rider on the road have? | A kite and a ball | A bell and a basket | *A helmet and a licence | A sandwich and a map
